    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1249">

                <pb facs="1477" n="1279" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/7–2545</note>
                <head>No. 1249<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                            Truman</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Whitehall</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Babelsberg</hi>]</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25">July 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>, I thank you for your
                    letter of July 25,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1249-f1"/>…</p>
                <p>I return the copy of the Proclamation to Japan by the Heads of Governments of the
                    United States, the United Kingdom, and the Republic of China, which I received
                    from you yesterday. I am willing to sign it on behalf of His Majesty’s
                    Government in its present form, and I hope you will issue it as you propose
                    whenever you choose and as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>On a minor point, I suggest that the word “industries” might be added where shown
                    in paragraph 11, otherwise the word “those” would seem at first sight to apply
                    to Separations.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1249-f2"/></p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winston S.
                                Churchill</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d1249-a1.xml" xpointer="d1249-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
